WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.730
Ugh, your head hurts,

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:05.600
you're nauseated, you're achy,

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:09.700
and you are certainly
never drinking again.

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:12.610
The only thought running
through your foggy mind is,

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:16.493
"Why are hangovers the absolute worst?"

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:21.830
Let's go back to last night.

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:26.760
As you down that
cocktail, alcohol migrates

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:29.320
through your GI tract to your liver,

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.730
where enzymes break it down.

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:34.760
But as you continue to drink,
your liver can't keep up.

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:37.850
So the alcohol overflows
into your bloodstream

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:41.920
and travels to other
organs like your brain.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:45.340
There, it suppresses a
hormone called vasopressin.

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:49.090
Normally, vasopressin prevents
you from urinating too much.

00:00:49.090 --> 00:00:52.670
So without it, you have
to pee all the time,

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:54.710
dehydrating you in the process,

00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:57.400
and that helps explain
your brutal headache

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:58.690
the next morning.

00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:01.430
But there are other chemicals at work,

00:01:01.430 --> 00:01:04.810
such as proinflammatory cytokines.

00:01:04.810 --> 00:01:08.050
These are small proteins
that stimulate inflammation,

00:01:08.050 --> 00:01:11.640
which causes symptoms like
nausea, jitters, and headaches.

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:12.900
And people who are hungover

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:15.010
have tons of them in their blood.

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:18.730
In fact, when researchers
injected proinflammatory cytokines

00:01:18.730 --> 00:01:21.290
into people who were stone-cold sober,

00:01:21.290 --> 00:01:25.702
they actually felt hungover
without all the fun beforehand.

00:01:25.702 --> 00:01:26.763
What a rip-off.

00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:30.590
Now, scientists aren't
exactly sure why binging

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:33.370
triggers this kind of
inflammatory response,

00:01:33.370 --> 00:01:35.770
but there is some evidence
that it's more severe

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:38.130
when you drink darker alcohols.

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:40.780
In one study, participants
who drank bourbon

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:43.790
instead of vodka reported
that their hangover symptoms

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:47.250
were 36% worse the next morning.

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:51.950
Then, there's that awful morning
anxiety called "hangxiety."

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:54.650
And no, it's not the guilt that you feel

00:01:54.650 --> 00:01:57.913
from all the bad decisions
you made the night before.

00:01:58.750 --> 00:02:01.060
It's actually biological.

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:04.000
Hangxiety starts to develop
when you finally put down

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:06.550
that last empty cocktail glass.

00:02:06.550 --> 00:02:08.680
You see, up until that point, your brain

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:11.490
has been ramping up the
activity of receptors

00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:15.693
called G-A-B-A, giving
you that calming buzz.

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:21.540
And at the same time, it's
been blocking glutamate,

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:24.090
a stimulant linked to anxiety.

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:25.610
But when you stop drinking,

00:02:25.610 --> 00:02:29.275
that whole system flips right around.

00:02:30.941 --> 00:02:33.900
Your brain empties those
calming G-A-B-A receptors

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:36.710
and floods with stimulating glutamate,

00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:39.440
which can make you feel abnormally anxious

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:41.650
by the time morning comes around.

00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:46.310
It can also disrupt your sleep
so you wake up still tired.

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:48.670
But enough with all that bad news.

00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:49.870
You want to know how you can make

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:53.550
that nasty hangover a thing of the past.

00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:56.490
Sorry to say, but that
delicious, greasy breakfast

00:02:56.490 --> 00:02:58.380
isn't doing you any favors.

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:02.650
Your body is running
low on water, not fat.

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:04.480
So your best bet is to hydrate

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:06.520
and take an anti-inflammatory.

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:10.620
Chances are the hangover
will vanish within 24 hours

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:13.319
or at least in time for next weekend.

00:03:13.319 --> 00:03:15.890
Uh, hello, my good friend?

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:18.240
Yes, I'd love to go to the big party,

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:21.083
and I will be drinking a
lot of alcohol as well.

